{#def
    settings: DownloadClientSettings,
#}

<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <h3 class="text-base">
        Download clients
    </h3>
    <p class="text-xs opacity-60">
        Optional, but much more reliable. Without one, a finished download is found by matching the
        release name against folder names, which fails when the client renames the folder. With one,
        Earr asks the client exactly where it put the files, and knows when a download is still
        running or has failed rather than guessing. Turn on the ones Prowlarr sends grabs to.
    </p>

    <form class="flex flex-col gap-2"
          hx-put="{{ base_url }}/settings/library/hx-download-clients"
          hx-disabled-elt="#dc-save">
        {% for client in settings.clients %}
            <details class="download-client group border-t border-base-200 pt-3"
                     {% if client.enabled %}open{% endif %}>
                <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-2">
                    <span class="font-semibold">
                        {{ client.name }}
                        <span class="text-xs font-normal opacity-60">({{ "torrents" if client.protocol == "torrent" else "usenet" }})</span>
                        {% if client.enabled %}<span class="badge badge-xs badge-success ml-1">on</span>{% endif %}
                    </span>
                    <input name="{{ client.id }}_enabled"
                           type="checkbox"
                           class="checkbox"
                           aria-label="Use {{ client.name }}"
                           onclick="event.stopPropagation()"
                           {% if client.enabled %}checked{% endif %} />
                </summary>
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 pt-2">
                    <input name="{{ client.id }}_url"
                           type="text"
                           value="{{ client.url }}"
                           placeholder="{{ {'qbit': 'http://192.168.0.102:8080', 'transmission': 'http://192.168.0.102:9091', 'deluge': 'http://192.168.0.102:8112', 'sab': 'http://192.168.0.103:8080', 'nzbget': 'http://192.168.0.103:6789'}[client.id] }}"
                           class="input w-full" />
                    <div class="flex gap-2">
                        {% if client.has_username %}
                            <input name="{{ client.id }}_username"
                                   type="text"
                                   value="{{ client.username }}"
                                   placeholder="username{{ ' (blank if the host is whitelisted)' if client.id == 'qbit' else '' }}"
                                   class="input w-full" />
                        {% endif %}
                        <input name="{{ client.id }}_secret"
                               type="password"
                               {% if client.secret_set %}placeholder="●●●●●●●● (unchanged)"{% else %}placeholder="{{ client.secret_label }}"{% endif %}
                               class="input w-full" />
                    </div>
                    {% if client.categories %}
                        <select name="{{ client.id }}_category" class="select w-full">
                            <option value="" {% if not client.category %}selected{% endif %}>
                                Leave the {{ "label" if client.id in ("transmission", "deluge") else "category" }} alone
                            </option>
                            {% for c in client.categories %}
                                <option value="{{ c }}" {% if client.category == c %}selected{% endif %}>{{ c }}</option>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </select>
                    {% else %}
                        <input name="{{ client.id }}_category"
                               type="text"
                               value="{{ client.category }}"
                               placeholder="{{ 'label' if client.id in ('transmission', 'deluge') else 'category' }} (optional)"
                               class="input w-full" />
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            </details>
        {% endfor %}

        <p class="text-xs opacity-60 pt-1">
            Prowlarr picks the category when it hands a release to the client and offers no way to
            override it, so Earr moves the download afterwards. In qBittorrent this relocates the
            files if the category has a save path and Auto Torrent Management is on, which is usually
            the point. Transmission and Deluge use labels (Deluge needs its Label plugin), and SABnzbd
            and NZBGet can only recategorise a job that is still in the queue.
        </p>

        <div class="flex gap-2 pt-2">
            <button id="dc-save" class="btn btn-primary">
                Save
            </button>
            <button type="button"
                    class="btn"
                    hx-post="{{ base_url }}/settings/library/hx-test-download-clients"
                    hx-disabled-elt="this">
                Test connection
            </button>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs opacity-60">
            Leave a password or API key blank to keep the stored one. Paths must look the same to Earr
            as they do to the client, which for Docker means mounting them the same way in both.
        </p>
    </form>
</div>
